 - **Shortened citations are DETECTED, never repaired (CCE-141).** `page-author` sometimes shortens an already-resolvable citation — the ADIS page cited `.claude/skills/connector-builder/references/checklist.md` at three sites and the rewrite emitted bare `references/checklist.md`, which `citation_exists` correctly blocked. Post-CCE-140 that is not a stall: the deferral skip abandons the PR and **the page is silently never written**. **What ships is diagnosis only.** `scripts/citation_repair.py` reports the tracked file such a citation was most likely shortened from and stops: `diagnose()` returns `[(cited, candidate, confidence)]`, there is no `Path.write_text` in the module, and **there must never be one** — do not restore `repair_text` or `rewrite_token`. Wired as `_diagnose_citation_paths` (`scripts/orchestrator_runner.py:1602`, called at `:2612` **after** the whole authoring loop and **above** the lint-block revert, so it reads the same finished tree `citation_exists` is about to read), `info_only`, one digest line per blocked citation. `diagnose` returns **four** labels — `candidate_in_run_inputs`, `suffix_match_only`, `ambiguous` (candidates capped at `_AMBIGUITY_CAP`, then `(+N more)`), `no_candidate` — but only **three** reach the digest: `no_candidate` is dropped, because its own evidence says the token is not a shortening of anything in the repo and `lint_block` already names those paths with severity. The other two used to `continue` **silently**, so a page blocked on two candidates produced no line at all while the single-candidate case was loud; the digest is now a census of blocked citations rather than a highlight reel. **Name the labels for what they measure.** They were `corroborated`/`uncorroborated` until round 5 — names that read as _confirmed_ while the status was granted by batch membership alone. `candidate_in_run_inputs` says only that an input to this run other than the authoring agent already named that file (rung 1: the linter's own `set(